Subject: renderer: replace the global operator new/delete only on request

tvgInitializer.cpp replaced the global operator new, new[], delete and delete[] (with
tvg::malloc and tvg::free, that is malloc and free). In a static library linked into an app, as
the iOS pod is, that replaces them for the whole app: every C++ allocation of React Native and
other libraries, and a link error with any other library that does the same. The replacement now
needs THORVG_GLOBAL_NEW; without it the standard operators are used, which call malloc and free
too.

Origin: Lordicon.
Base: thorvg/thorvg main 72a66415 (1.2.0). License: MIT, like ThorVG.
---
diff --git a/src/renderer/tvgInitializer.cpp b/src/renderer/tvgInitializer.cpp
--- a/src/renderer/tvgInitializer.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer/tvgInitializer.cpp
@@ -138,6 +138,10 @@
 }
 
 
+// Replacing the global operators is the application's choice: in a static library (an iOS pod)
+// it would replace them for the whole app, and clash with any other library that does too.
+#ifdef THORVG_GLOBAL_NEW
+
 void* operator new(std::size_t size)
 {
     return tvg::malloc(size);
@@ -160,3 +164,5 @@
 {
     tvg::free(ptr);
 }
+
+#endif
